  "caveats": [
    "Deterministic stub model, not a live LLM. A real model would add sampling noise larger than the effect being measured; the stub isolates the memory layer and makes every number reproducible. It is not a strawman: it answers knowledge-free tasks correctly in both arms, so injected context can only hurt on those.",
    "MEASURED: every token count is the real size of the real prompt the pipeline assembled, including the accumulating transcript and the block the SDK injected. Recall is a real call through the gateway against a store of hundreds of memories, and when it ranks the wrong memory first the task fails and is counted as a failure.",
    "MODELLED: how many documents an agent that does not know the answer reads before finding it (in-order scan, no backtracking or re-reading \u2014 favourable to the baseline), and that missing knowledge costs a bounded amount of rework rather than an unbounded amount (also favourable to the baseline).",
    "Synthetic workload, authored alongside the product. It demonstrates a mechanism \u2014 what carrying knowledge between runs does to accuracy and cost \u2014 not a market-wide claim. 44% of the suite is tasks no memory layer can help with, and they are in the headline aggregate rather than excluded from it.",
    "Both arms run identical inputs through identical SDK and gateway code, with no privileged channel by which the informed arm learns anything the wrapper did not put in the prompt."
  ]
